mpegv.library/--background--                   mpegv.library/--background--

    PURPOSE
        Decodes MPEG-1 video (a .mpg Program Stream, a VCD's .dat, a bare
        .m1v stream) by the CPU, for any program, as mpega.library decodes
        MPEG audio. A 68020 or better; no FPU needed.

        The decoder is pl_mpeg (Dominic Szablewski), made about 2.6 times
        faster on a 68020 than it was, its pictures the same bit for bit.
        A VCD's picture (352 x 240) takes about 11 million 68020 cycles
        (vamos's count); an emulated 68060 decoded one in about 4 ms, well
        inside the 33 ms a picture lasts. A 68030 or 68020 is too slow for
        every picture: pass B pictures over (MpvControl's MPVC_SKIPB).

    USE
        Open a decoder (MpvOpen) with a read hook that gives it the
        stream's bytes, and, for a Program Stream, a packet hook that is
        given its other packets (its sound: MPEG audio for mpega.library,
        private stream 1 for ac3.library). Then MpvDecode, again and
        again: each picture in display order, the decoder's own Y, Cb and
        Cr planes (4:2:0, not copied), with its time in 90 kHz ticks. Show
        it with a helper: MpvToYUV422 for a graphics card's overlay
        (Picasso96's PIP), MpvToRGB to draw (WritePixelArray), MpvToGrey
        for an AGA screen of greys (WriteChunkyPixels or your own c2p).

        Without a read hook the program gives the bytes itself (MpvWrite)
        whenever MpvDecode answers MPVE_MORE, and says when there are no
        more (MpvControl MPVC_END).

        A decoder is used by one task at a time; different decoders may be
        used by different tasks at once. The helpers may be called by any
        task (they use only the picture they are given).

    HOOKS
        Called as the Amiga calls hooks: A0 the hook, A2 the decoder, A1
        the message; with the calling task's stack. In C (gcc):

        ULONG read(register struct Hook *h __asm("a0"),
                   register APTR mpv __asm("a2"),
                   register struct MpvRead *r __asm("a1"))

        The read hook may be called during MpvOpen (a Program Stream's
        first headers are read at once), and during MpvDecode, MpvPump and
        MpvGetInfo. The packet hook, during MpvDecode and MpvPump.

    TIMES
        All 90 kHz ticks, integers, as MPEG stores them. A picture's
        mpic_Time counts from the first picture's (its number times the
        frame period, exactly: 3003 ticks a picture at 29.97); mpic_PTS adds
        the stream's first video time stamp (a Program Stream's), to set it
        beside its sound's (struct MpvPacket's mp_PTS).

    MEMORY
        About 3 pictures' planes and two 128 KB buffers a decoder (a VCD:
        about 640 KB), from exec (MEMF_ANY).

    LIBRARIES
        Opens mathieeedoubbas.library (pl_mpeg keeps a picture's and a
        packet's time in floating point too, a division each) and, if it
        is there, mathieeesingbas.library.

    LICENCE
        MIT (LICENSE): the library, its interface and pl_mpeg alike.

mpegv.library/MpvClose                               mpegv.library/MpvClose

    NAME
        MpvClose -- a decoder freed (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        MpvClose(mpv)
                 A0
        VOID MpvClose(APTR);

    FUNCTION
        Frees a decoder from MpvOpen and its pictures. NULL is ignored.

mpegv.library/MpvControl                           mpegv.library/MpvControl

    NAME
        MpvControl -- a setting changed, or a count read (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        result = MpvControl(mpv, cmd, value)
        D0                  A0   D0   D1
        LONG MpvControl(APTR, ULONG, ULONG);

    FUNCTION
        MPVC_SKIPB      value TRUE: B pictures passed over from here, not
                        decoded (nothing is predicted from them: a VCD's
                        are two in three); FALSE: decoded again. Their
                        times still count. Returns the last setting.
        MPVC_SKIPPEDB   returns how many B pictures were passed over.
        MPVC_ENDED      returns TRUE once the stream's end was reached.
        MPVC_FIRSTPTS   returns the first video time stamp (90 kHz), or
                        -1 if none has been read.
        MPVC_END        (without a read hook) no more bytes will come:
                        what is held is decoded, then MPVE_END.
        MPVC_HELD       returns the bytes held, read but not yet decoded.

mpegv.library/MpvDecode                             mpegv.library/MpvDecode

    NAME
        MpvDecode -- the next picture (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        pic = MpvDecode(mpv, error)
        D0              A0   A1
        struct MpvPicture *MpvDecode(APTR, LONG *);

    FUNCTION
        Decodes up to the next picture in display order, reading what it
        needs (the read hook, or what MpvWrite gave). The picture is the
        decoder's own: valid until the next MpvDecode or MpvClose.

    RESULT
        The picture, or NULL with *error (if error is not NULL):
        MPVE_END    the stream's end
        MPVE_MORE   no picture yet: call again (without a read hook,
                    after MpvWrite)
        MPVE_READ   the read hook said it could not read
        MPVE_STREAM not an MPEG-1 stream mpegv decodes

mpegv.library/MpvGetInfo                           mpegv.library/MpvGetInfo

    NAME
        MpvGetInfo -- the stream's size and pace (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        ok = MpvGetInfo(mpv, info)
        D0              A0   A1
        LONG MpvGetInfo(APTR, struct MpvInfo *);

    FUNCTION
        Fills info from the stream's sequence header (read first if it
        has not been): its size, its pictures a second (mi_RateNum /
        mi_RateDen, and mi_Period in 90 kHz ticks), its pixels' shape
        (mi_AspectCode, and mi_ShownWidth: its width for its height as it
        is meant to be seen), its bit rate, and what kind of stream it
        turned out to be.

    RESULT
        TRUE, or FALSE if no sequence header could be read (yet).

mpegv.library/MpvOpen                                 mpegv.library/MpvOpen

    NAME
        MpvOpen -- a decoder (V1)
        MpvOpenTags -- the same, its tags as arguments

    SYNOPSIS
        mpv = MpvOpen(tags)
        D0            A0
        APTR MpvOpen(struct TagItem *);

        mpv = MpvOpenTags(tag1, ...)
        APTR MpvOpenTags(Tag, ...);

    FUNCTION
        A decoder for one stream.

    TAGS
        MPVA_ReadHook (struct Hook *) - the stream's bytes: the hook is
            given a struct MpvRead (mr_Buffer, mr_Length) and returns how
            many it put there, 0 at the end, -1 if it could not read.
            Without one, give the bytes with MpvWrite.
        MPVA_PacketHook (struct Hook *) - each packet of a Program Stream
            that is not its video: a struct MpvPacket (its stream id, its
            time if it has one, its bytes: valid during the call).
        MPVA_Stream (ULONG) - MPVS_PROGRAM, MPVS_VIDEO, or MPVS_AUTO (the
            default: a pack header or a sequence header first says).
        MPVA_ReadSize (ULONG) - bytes asked of the read hook at once
            (default 16384, at least 2048).
        MPVA_SkipB (BOOL) - B pictures passed over from the start.

    RESULT
        The decoder, or NULL (no memory; or the read hook failed at once).

mpegv.library/MpvPump                                 mpegv.library/MpvPump

    NAME
        MpvPump -- one more packet demultiplexed (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        more = MpvPump(mpv)
        D0             A0
        LONG MpvPump(APTR);

    FUNCTION
        A Program Stream's next packet: video to the decoder (held until
        MpvDecode wants it), anything else to the packet hook. For a
        program that wants its sound ahead of the pictures (mpega.library
        reading from a queue the packet hook fills): when the queue is
        empty, MpvPump until it is not.

    RESULT
        TRUE, or FALSE at the stream's end (or, without a read hook, when
        it wants more bytes; or for a bare video stream).

mpegv.library/MpvToGrey                             mpegv.library/MpvToGrey

    NAME
        MpvToGrey -- a picture made 8-bit greys (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        MpvToGrey(pic, dst, modulo, levels)
                  A0   A1   D0      D1
        VOID MpvToGrey(struct MpvPicture *, UBYTE *, ULONG, ULONG);

    FUNCTION
        Writes mpic_Width x mpic_Height bytes at dst, modulo bytes a row:
        each pixel's brightness, full range 0-255 (levels 0 or 256), or
        0 to levels - 1 (a screen's grey pens, its palette set to match).
        For an AGA screen: WriteChunkyPixels (graphics.library 40), or a
        chunky-to-planar routine.

mpegv.library/MpvToRGB                               mpegv.library/MpvToRGB

    NAME
        MpvToRGB -- a picture made RGB (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        MpvToRGB(pic, dst, modulo, format)
                 A0   A1   D0      D1
        VOID MpvToRGB(struct MpvPicture *, UBYTE *, ULONG, ULONG);

    FUNCTION
        Writes the picture at dst, modulo bytes a row, in format:
        MPVR_RGB24 and MPVR_BGR24 (3 bytes a pixel), MPVR_ARGB32,
        MPVR_RGBA32 and MPVR_BGRA32 (4, alpha 0xFF), MPVR_RGB565 (big-
        endian), MPVR_RGB565PC (little-endian) and MPVR_RGB555 (2).
        BT.601, as pl_mpeg converts. MPVR_RGB24 is WritePixelArray's
        RECTFMT_RGB, MPVR_ARGB32 its RECTFMT_ARGB.

mpegv.library/MpvToYUV422                         mpegv.library/MpvToYUV422

    NAME
        MpvToYUV422 -- a picture made packed YUV 4:2:2 (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        MpvToYUV422(pic, dst, modulo, order)
                    A0   A1   D0      D1
        VOID MpvToYUV422(struct MpvPicture *, UBYTE *, ULONG, ULONG);

    FUNCTION
        Writes the picture at dst, modulo bytes a row, two pixels a
        longword (each chroma row twice): for a graphics card's overlay,
        which scales it (Picasso96's PIP: p96PIP_OpenTags, then
        p96LockBitMap its P96PIP_SourceBitMap and write here). A
        longword at a time: the card's memory across the bus.
        order: MPVY_Y0UY1V (Y0 Cb Y1 Cr: RGBFB_YUV422CGX as the ZZ9000
        shows it), MPVY_UY0VY1, MPVY_Y1UY0V (RGBFB_YUV422), MPVY_Y0VY1U.
        Which a card wants for which format is the card's driver's: try
        them on yours.

mpegv.library/MpvVersion                           mpegv.library/MpvVersion

    NAME
        MpvVersion -- the library's version, in words (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        text = MpvVersion()
        D0
        CONST_STRPTR MpvVersion(void);

mpegv.library/MpvWrite                               mpegv.library/MpvWrite

    NAME
        MpvWrite -- the stream's next bytes given (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        taken = MpvWrite(mpv, buf, len)
        D0               A0   A1   D0
        LONG MpvWrite(APTR, CONST UBYTE *, LONG);

    FUNCTION
        Without a read hook: len more bytes of the stream (copied).
        Typically when MpvDecode answers MPVE_MORE.

    RESULT
        len, or 0 after MPVC_END.
